# The runnable bundle: NetBox, PostgreSQL, Garnet, the .NET runtime and Python.
#
# Around 620 MB across 30,000 files, and none of it is ours - it is third-party
# software downloaded and assembled by the build scripts. Keeping it out of the
# repository is deliberate:
#
#   * build/components.json pins every component with its SHA256, so
#     build\fetch-components.ps1 followed by build\build-bundle.ps1 reproduces
#     it byte for byte
#   * a repository carrying redistributed upstream binaries is awkward to
#     license, slow to clone and quick to go stale
#
# Ship the built MSI as a GitHub release asset instead of committing it.
dist/

# Build tooling fetched on demand (WiX Toolset).
build/tools/
build/cache/

# Generated by heat.exe from the payload directory; regenerated on every build.
installer/Files.wxs
installer/obj/

# Local editor and OS noise.
.vs/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Python bytecode. Regenerated at runtime, and its long file names run into the
# Windows 260 character path limit during packaging.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Never commit these: local credentials and a configuration that carries the
# database password of whichever machine last ran the instance.
**/netbox/netbox/configuration.py
secrets/
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
.env
